From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] linker: fall back only to a VNDK APEX that is actually
 mounted

The fallback for a vendor whose sepolicy version is not its VNDK version
picked the oldest com.android.vndk.v* name in /apex at or above the
sepolicy version, and only then checked whether its library directory
resolved. A name in /apex is not a mounted APEX: mount-android.sh now
mounts only the vendor's own VNDK APEX on the host, and the other
versions can be left as empty directories.

On the FuriPhone FLX1s (radon: sepolicy 31.0, ro.vndk.version 32) an
empty com.android.vndk.v31 sat next to a mounted v32. v31 won the scan,
matched the sepolicy version, so the fallback was skipped and the lookup
returned nothing. HYBRIS_PREFER_VNDK then did nothing, and pulseaudio
died on the android::base::Basename that libnvram.so needs, as it did
before the fallback existed (read on the device, 14 Nov 2026).

Check each candidate's library directory while scanning, and take the
oldest one that resolves.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 common/q/linker.cpp | 26 +++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/q/linker.cpp b/common/q/linker.cpp
index 870f06d..0e850d8 100644
--- a/common/q/linker.cpp
+++ b/common/q/linker.cpp
@@ -1249,11 +1249,18 @@ static const std::string& vndk_apex_lib_dir() {
     // So use what is on the filesystem: the oldest APEX at least as new as the
     // sepolicy version. VNDK APEXes are backward compatible for older vendors,
     // and taking the oldest such keeps a v34 from being preferred over a v32.
+    //
+    // Only an APEX whose library directory resolves counts. A name in /apex
+    // is not a mounted APEX: the host mounts only the vendor's own VNDK APEX,
+    // and the other versions can be left as empty directories. On radon an
+    // empty com.android.vndk.v31 next to a mounted v32 won the scan, matched
+    // the sepolicy version, and so the lookup returned nothing at all.
     long want = strtol(version.c_str(), nullptr, 10);
     if (want > 0) {
       DIR* apex_dir = opendir("/apex");
       if (apex_dir != nullptr) {
         long best = 0;
+        std::string best_path;
         static const char kPrefix[] = "com.android.vndk.v";
         struct dirent* ent;
         while ((ent = readdir(apex_dir)) != nullptr) {
@@ -1261,17 +1268,18 @@ static const std::string& vndk_apex_lib_dir() {
           const char* digits = ent->d_name + sizeof(kPrefix) - 1;
           if (*digits < '0' || *digits > '9') continue;
           long have = strtol(digits, nullptr, 10);
-          if (have >= want && (best == 0 || have < best)) best = have;
+          if (have < want || (best != 0 && have >= best)) continue;
+          std::string fallback = std::string("/apex/com.android.vndk.v") +
+                                 std::to_string(have) + kApexLibDirSuffix;
+          if (realpath(fallback.c_str(), real_path) == nullptr) continue;
+          best = have;
+          best_path = real_path;
         }
         closedir(apex_dir);
-        if (best != 0 && best != want) {
-          std::string fallback = std::string("/apex/com.android.vndk.v") +
-                                 std::to_string(best) + kApexLibDirSuffix;
-          if (realpath(fallback.c_str(), real_path) != nullptr) {
-            DL_WARN("hybris: no VNDK APEX v%ld (sepolicy says %s), using v%ld",
-                    want, version.c_str(), best);
-            return std::string(real_path);
-          }
+        if (best != 0) {
+          DL_WARN("hybris: no VNDK APEX v%ld (sepolicy says %s), using v%ld",
+                  want, version.c_str(), best);
+          return best_path;
         }
       }
     }
